WEBVTT

00:01.230 --> 00:03.730
I challenge you to a one-on-one.

00:06.940 --> 00:10.030
<i>That's a captain's uniform.</i>

00:18.160 --> 00:20.490
A one-on-one.

00:25.520 --> 00:28.650
Make them see that halation!

00:28.650 --> 00:32.070
We'll carry out the oath we made that day.

00:32.070 --> 00:35.110
Spread out, new formation!

00:35.110 --> 00:38.620
We can see the signs as we call out for one another.

00:38.620 --> 00:44.870
Place your hopes in it, shoot, and watch the arch!

00:45.160 --> 00:49.790
I believe in you, do it like you always do.

00:49.790 --> 00:51.460
Leave it to me.

00:51.460 --> 00:58.010
Put your hands on your chest, and calm yourself down.

00:58.010 --> 01:04.350
I remember each and every granted wish,

01:04.350 --> 01:10.230
including that day I cried in secret.

01:10.230 --> 01:13.690
We're not the only ones

01:13.690 --> 01:17.280
seeing these same dreams.

01:17.280 --> 01:20.910
The sparks in those unyielding eyes

01:20.910 --> 01:24.040
that appeared in front of me,

01:24.040 --> 01:25.580
let them fly!

01:25.870 --> 01:29.000
Make them see that halation!

01:29.000 --> 01:32.380
Run into that open space!

01:32.380 --> 01:39.010
This lingering sensation, looking back on those carefree days.

01:39.010 --> 01:45.560
After saying farewell, you smile with everyone else,

01:45.560 --> 01:51.810
aim for the place you dreamed of, shoot, and watch the arch!

01:54.000 --> 01:58.510
Flying Match!

02:01.010 --> 02:02.300
Good.

02:10.980 --> 02:11.650
<i>A feint!</i>

02:13.400 --> 02:17.440
<i>Tomoka may have seen through her feint, but that girl's still good.</i>

02:22.370 --> 02:25.330
I'll show you something too.

02:33.960 --> 02:35.590
A-Are you okay?

02:35.590 --> 02:36.380
Thanks.

02:38.630 --> 02:40.340
It's your turn to be on the offense.

02:51.020 --> 02:52.150
<i>Now's my chance!</i>

02:53.650 --> 02:54.940
Great play!

03:13.500 --> 03:14.960
I fouled.

03:14.960 --> 03:16.460
Basket count.

03:16.460 --> 03:17.800
You get a free throw.

03:17.800 --> 03:20.220
You barely touched me, though.

03:20.220 --> 03:21.630
Take it.

03:36.690 --> 03:38.070
Beautiful...

03:43.410 --> 03:45.490
I lost to a girl.

03:45.490 --> 03:47.950
My first time, to her...

03:48.240 --> 03:50.080
I-I'm really sorry!

03:50.080 --> 03:52.960
I thought that it would be rude if I didn't take it seriously!

03:53.960 --> 03:56.710
Gotta say, that was terrific.

03:56.710 --> 03:58.550
What a spectacle that was.

03:59.420 --> 04:01.050
D-Dad!

04:01.670 --> 04:03.380
It's been a while, Son.

04:03.590 --> 04:04.510
Oh man!

04:04.510 --> 04:05.550
When did you get back?

04:05.550 --> 04:07.680
I got into Narita a little while ago.

04:07.680 --> 04:08.720
Where's Nayu Nayu?

04:08.720 --> 04:11.020
Mom's inside.

04:11.770 --> 04:12.890
By the way...

04:13.270 --> 04:14.770
My name is Mimi Balguerie.

04:14.770 --> 04:16.310
Nice to meet you.

04:16.310 --> 04:18.150
She's my precious child.

04:18.150 --> 04:19.070
Be nice to her.

04:22.320 --> 04:24.070
So that's what you meant.

04:24.070 --> 04:27.200
So Mimi-chan's your pupil.

04:27.200 --> 04:28.330
Yep.

04:28.330 --> 04:31.040
Mimi's the daughter of a French professor who worked with me

04:31.040 --> 04:33.710
during the Hawaii excavation project I was participating in.

04:33.710 --> 04:37.250
I was asked to coach her in basketball during my stay.

04:37.790 --> 04:39.960
You're coaching, huh?

04:39.960 --> 04:43.420
Yeah, and I haven't not lost my touch whatsoever!

04:43.420 --> 04:45.760
Ginga-kun was really good!

04:45.760 --> 04:49.310
Shiba Academy's male
basketball team's legendary ace.

04:49.310 --> 04:51.560
You're flattering me, Nayu Nayu!

04:51.560 --> 04:52.930
Oh, am I?

04:52.930 --> 04:54.690
Yes you are, Nayu Nayu!

04:54.690 --> 04:56.060
Those lovebirds...

04:54.690 --> 04:56.520
Am I really, Ginga-kun?

05:03.030 --> 05:04.990
Tomo or Chika?

05:04.990 --> 05:07.820
Ah, um, it's Tomoka.

05:08.530 --> 05:11.700
Tomoka, your breasts are a little big.

05:11.700 --> 05:13.370
Y-You think so?

05:13.370 --> 05:16.620
I'm still as flat and smooth as a board...

05:16.620 --> 05:19.630
But Mimi-chan, you're still a fifth year.

05:19.630 --> 05:21.590
You'll get bigger soon.

05:22.000 --> 05:23.710
I can't wait.

05:25.300 --> 05:26.300
Tomoka!

05:26.300 --> 05:27.470
Y-Yes?

05:27.680 --> 05:31.180
I hope we can have another match again soon.

05:32.720 --> 05:34.100
Indeed.

05:34.100 --> 05:35.180
I'd love to.

05:38.650 --> 05:40.690
You're making me jealous, Mokkan.

05:40.690 --> 05:44.320
Getting involved in something
so interesting right at the end of summer.

05:44.530 --> 05:45.240
Yep.

05:45.240 --> 05:49.200
Mimi-chan was really good at basketball and I had a blast.

05:49.200 --> 05:51.240
I heard she's still going to be in Japan for some time.

05:51.580 --> 05:55.500
So maybe we can meet her if we ask Hasegawa-san?

05:55.660 --> 05:59.500
Oh! I would love to meet Onii-chan's papa, too!

05:59.500 --> 06:01.090
What kind of person is he?

06:01.090 --> 06:03.420
He's a wonderful father.

06:03.420 --> 06:06.220
He also knows a lot about basketball.

06:06.220 --> 06:07.260
Nee-sama.

06:08.470 --> 06:09.890
Ah, Kage-chan.

06:09.890 --> 06:12.350
Oh! What is it, Kage?

06:12.350 --> 06:13.390
Um...

06:14.600 --> 06:15.720
Mimi-chan!

06:15.720 --> 06:17.180
What? So that's Mimi?

06:17.600 --> 06:20.150
She got transferred into my class.

06:20.980 --> 06:24.190
She wanted to say hello when I talked about everyone.

06:24.440 --> 06:25.400
Yeah.

06:25.400 --> 06:27.950
I heard everyone here plays basketball.

06:27.950 --> 06:29.700
I hope to play with everyone too.

06:29.700 --> 06:31.870
O-Of course, it'd be our pleasure.

06:31.870 --> 06:33.780
Well then, let's get going.

06:33.780 --> 06:34.620
Yeah.

06:34.620 --> 06:35.660
See you.

06:41.080 --> 06:42.960
She's like a doll!

06:42.960 --> 06:43.920
Yeah!

06:46.460 --> 06:48.840
We need to plan a gathering soon.

06:49.550 --> 06:52.220
Yeah, we weren't able to get
together during the summer break.

06:52.220 --> 06:55.890
I need to start studying for my exams soon, though.

06:55.890 --> 06:56.970
So early!

06:56.970 --> 06:58.390
You're gonna start studying already?

06:58.680 --> 07:02.900
Yeah, like, I probably can't make it.

07:03.440 --> 07:05.110
I'll invite a few people for you though.

07:05.110 --> 07:07.530
Well, that would help a lot, but...

07:07.530 --> 07:08.900
You have any good ideas?

07:09.190 --> 07:11.450
Well, I'll try and ask around.

07:12.820 --> 07:13.910
All right!

07:14.490 --> 07:16.240
Let's concentrate and brace ourselves for another day!

07:16.660 --> 07:18.120
Yeah!

07:19.750 --> 07:21.500
Nii-tan's so cool!

07:21.920 --> 07:23.500
Look here!

07:23.500 --> 07:25.090
Look in our direction!

07:26.380 --> 07:28.960
Hey, Takki. They're here again.

07:28.960 --> 07:32.550
Your little sisters are as full of energy as usual.

07:32.550 --> 07:35.430
I thought I told them not to
come during my club activity...

07:37.430 --> 07:39.100
I have come to ask a favor!

07:39.730 --> 07:40.560
Huh?

07:40.560 --> 07:42.980
Isn't that Hakamada's younger sister?

07:42.980 --> 07:45.110
Who's that beside her?

07:49.440 --> 07:50.190
What is it?

07:50.190 --> 07:51.570
What are you here for?

07:51.570 --> 07:54.410
Um, well...

07:54.410 --> 07:56.910
The Dojo challenge, was it?

07:56.910 --> 07:57.580
Huh?

07:58.120 --> 08:00.750
The basketball club shall be mine!

08:00.750 --> 08:03.330
Captain, I challenge you to a one-on-one!

08:03.830 --> 08:05.290
Hey, what are you even say—

08:05.290 --> 08:06.500
U-Um...

08:06.500 --> 08:10.090
I think Mimi-san wants her own team.

08:10.090 --> 08:10.960
A team?

08:11.420 --> 08:15.090
Apparently, she had a match with Tomoka-senpai the other day.

08:15.090 --> 08:17.890
And she wants a rematch.

08:17.890 --> 08:18.810
That's why...

08:19.010 --> 08:20.640
"That's why," what?

08:21.350 --> 08:24.480
Mimi-san intends to gain control of the male basketball club

08:24.480 --> 08:26.980
and challenge the female basketball club...

08:26.980 --> 08:28.070
What?

08:28.070 --> 08:29.110
What the heck are you saying?

08:29.940 --> 08:31.610
I'm sorry! Please forgive me!

08:31.610 --> 08:34.320
I can't have a match with Tomoka if we're on the same team.

08:34.820 --> 08:36.570
I need a different team.

08:37.530 --> 08:39.700
I don't think I can help you with that...

08:44.540 --> 08:44.670
You've got mail!

08:44.790 --> 08:44.920
Fujii Masami

08:45.420 --> 08:45.560
Subject:

08:45.420 --> 08:45.560
A burning
passion revealed!

08:45.560 --> 08:45.650
Subject:

08:48.500 --> 08:50.800
What do you think that is?

08:51.130 --> 08:52.300
Masami.

08:52.300 --> 08:53.260
This is...

08:53.260 --> 08:54.970
A burning passion revealed!

08:54.970 --> 08:56.800
That photo's your treasure, isn't it?

08:57.340 --> 09:00.810
I shall distribute that around the Suzuran shopping district

09:00.810 --> 09:05.100
and bring down the image of you and your family.

09:07.350 --> 09:10.400
Doing something like that will amount to nothing, though.

09:11.530 --> 09:15.070
Keep your composure while you still can.

09:15.070 --> 09:16.530
Goodbye for now!

09:18.990 --> 09:20.280
Seriously...

09:29.330 --> 09:30.420
Hello?

09:30.420 --> 09:31.630
Saki here.

09:31.630 --> 09:35.090
Um, I have something to
inform you of, Hasegawa-san.

09:35.090 --> 09:36.010
What is it?

09:36.260 --> 09:42.600
Well, it seems that I got my photo taken by
my childhood friend at the summer festival.

09:42.600 --> 09:43.520
Photo?

09:43.520 --> 09:44.470
Yes.

09:44.470 --> 09:48.060
It was when you were teaching me how to shoot properly.

09:48.060 --> 09:49.520
I'll send it to you.

09:49.900 --> 09:51.610
The shooting range?

09:51.610 --> 09:52.690
But why?

09:54.480 --> 09:57.320
Wh-What is this "A burning
passion revealed!" all about?

10:00.120 --> 10:01.280
Hello, Saki?

10:01.280 --> 10:02.080
This photo...

10:02.240 --> 10:06.120
Well, I don't think anyone would think that way about it,

10:06.120 --> 10:08.960
but I didn't want to take any chances and end up causing you trouble,

10:09.290 --> 10:13.130
so I'm thinking of asking
Masami to delete the photo.

10:13.130 --> 10:14.880
<i>Th-This is bad.</i>

10:14.880 --> 10:18.220
<i>If by any chance a bad rumor gets spread...</i>

10:21.800 --> 10:23.390
That's the rumored lolicon coach.

10:22.850 --> 10:24.260
What a pervert.

10:23.810 --> 10:25.810
Apparently, he was heard saying
"Elementary schoolers are the best!".

10:26.810 --> 10:27.980
This is awesome!

10:28.270 --> 10:30.190
S-Saki, I'm going as well!

10:30.190 --> 10:30.650
Huh?

10:30.650 --> 10:32.060
I'll be right there, so wait for me!

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
Date of birth

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
Blood type

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
Class

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
5th Year, Class D

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
Height

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
Name

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
Bust size

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
Rival

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
Minato Tomoka

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
Totally flat. I hope they grow quicker.

10:40.110 --> 10:43.080
Mimi Balguerie

10:44.740 --> 10:47.040
Thank you for coming all this way.

10:47.330 --> 10:48.710
I-It's fine.

10:48.710 --> 10:50.420
But how did something like this happen?

10:50.830 --> 10:54.170
Masami's my childhood friend,
and she's younger than me by a year.

10:54.170 --> 10:56.210
Our families are on good terms with each other,

10:56.760 --> 11:00.180
but she started to dislike me one day.

11:00.590 --> 11:06.520
My family's shop, Nagatsuka, took first place on our local shopping district's magazine.

11:06.520 --> 11:10.060
Masami's family runs a sushi shop called Sushi Fuji,

11:10.060 --> 11:11.850
and they got second place.

11:12.270 --> 11:13.860
I'm seeing the picture now.

11:13.860 --> 11:16.860
But Sushi Fuji only got second
because it's somewhat high class,

11:16.860 --> 11:19.030
so the votes went somewhere else.

11:19.030 --> 11:22.070
In any case, let's have a talk with Masami-san.

11:22.450 --> 11:23.370
Yes, let's.

11:29.450 --> 11:30.290
Masami!

11:31.920 --> 11:33.580
I knew you'd be here.

11:33.580 --> 11:37.300
You'd always be here when you receive something you like.

11:38.170 --> 11:39.510
Shut it!

11:39.510 --> 11:41.590
So you guys really <i>were</i> dating!

11:42.220 --> 11:43.470
No, we aren't.

11:43.470 --> 11:45.930
We're just here to clear up the misunderstanding.

11:46.390 --> 11:48.600
I have nothing to say to you.

11:48.600 --> 11:51.940
It'll be the end of you the
moment I send this photo out.

11:53.690 --> 11:54.520
Is that so?

11:54.520 --> 11:56.230
Do as you wish then.

11:57.520 --> 11:59.110
R-Really?

12:01.400 --> 12:05.450
Well then, I shall go and claim the top place in Suzuran right away.

12:06.620 --> 12:07.620
The top, huh?

12:09.040 --> 12:12.710
And what is it that makes you so
confident that your shop will beat ours?

12:12.710 --> 12:13.960
What do you mean by that?

12:14.290 --> 12:18.130
Even if that photo gets spread around and our reputation is tarnished,

12:18.130 --> 12:20.960
it doesn't mean Sushi Fuji's
reputation is going to improve.

12:22.510 --> 12:26.180
Instead of improving, rumors of
them using underhanded methods

12:26.180 --> 12:29.680
might spread and result in
you destroying their image.

12:31.730 --> 12:34.310
S-Stop acting like you know everything!

12:35.230 --> 12:35.350
Deleted

12:35.350 --> 12:35.480
Deleted

12:35.480 --> 12:36.100
Deleted

12:36.100 --> 12:37.110
Deleted

12:37.110 --> 12:37.230
Deleted

12:37.360 --> 12:38.610
Just you watch.

12:38.610 --> 12:43.110
Even without doing something like this, we'll definitely take the top this year.

12:47.240 --> 12:48.530
Thanks, Saki.

12:48.870 --> 12:49.870
Not at all.

12:49.870 --> 12:54.120
I was actually afraid that it might have failed.

12:54.870 --> 12:56.330
By the way, Saki.

12:56.330 --> 12:57.170
What is it?

12:57.880 --> 13:01.170
Does Masami play basketball?

13:01.170 --> 13:02.670
Ah, no...

13:03.470 --> 13:05.180
Well, she was wearing basketball shoes.

13:05.550 --> 13:08.180
No, I don't think she plays.

13:08.930 --> 13:10.140
I see.

13:13.930 --> 13:18.440
Nii-tan should just join forces with Mimi and defeat stupid Maho.

13:18.440 --> 13:19.860
Yes, you should!

13:20.270 --> 13:23.860
Even <i>we're<i> better than stupid Maho.</i></i>

13:24.280 --> 13:26.860
I'm okay with anything as long as I'm in the match.

13:28.660 --> 13:29.870
Say, Kagetsu.

13:30.370 --> 13:33.830
Is it true that you practice
basketball with Hinata sometimes?

13:33.830 --> 13:35.960
Huh? Ah, yes.

13:35.960 --> 13:38.420
Practicing passes and dribbles.

13:38.420 --> 13:40.250
Jogging together too.

13:40.710 --> 13:42.670
Hinata sang praises about you,

13:42.670 --> 13:45.220
about how you have been improving really fast.

13:45.220 --> 13:47.380
Onee-sama said that?

13:47.760 --> 13:51.760
W-Well, I just happened to overhear her talking.

13:54.770 --> 13:55.890
By the way,

13:56.480 --> 14:00.400
what would you do if you were to have a match with Hinata?

14:04.900 --> 14:07.860
Oh! That scrubbing feels great

14:09.280 --> 14:10.990
Oh!

14:14.700 --> 14:15.870
Oh!

14:18.750 --> 14:21.750
U-Um, Nee-sama?

14:21.750 --> 14:22.630
Huh?

14:23.000 --> 14:27.510
If you had to battle against me, what would you think?

14:27.510 --> 14:29.630
Fighting's not good.

14:29.630 --> 14:31.340
No, not an actual fight.

14:31.340 --> 14:34.060
Oh! Let' see who can hold their breath the longest.

14:50.740 --> 14:53.660
Hina thinks a battle with Kage would be fun.

14:54.240 --> 14:55.740
Nee-sama!

15:06.420 --> 15:10.180
Doing your usual long-shot practice?

15:10.180 --> 15:12.800
I just felt like doing it.

15:13.180 --> 15:16.260
That handmade hoop used to be mine, though.

15:16.970 --> 15:18.980
I'm sorry for using it without permission.

15:18.980 --> 15:19.940
It's fine.

15:19.940 --> 15:22.190
Anyone who wants to improve themselves can use it.

15:22.690 --> 15:26.520
You've been here every morning
since summer break, haven't you?

15:27.900 --> 15:28.780
And?

15:28.780 --> 15:32.610
How do you intend to show off your skills to Saki?

15:32.610 --> 15:33.660
H-How did you know that?

15:34.030 --> 15:35.450
It's pretty widespread.

15:35.450 --> 15:38.160
You and your rivalry with Saki.

15:41.080 --> 15:42.460
Don't you want to have a match?

15:45.210 --> 15:47.250
With Saki, at basketball.

15:49.800 --> 15:51.340
We're here for a favor!

15:52.130 --> 15:53.180
Mimi-chan!

15:53.180 --> 15:54.510
TsubaHii?

15:54.890 --> 15:57.180
Don't call us TsubaHii, stupid Maho!

15:57.180 --> 15:59.390
We fifth years have banded together

15:59.390 --> 16:02.020
to dojo challenge you female basketballers!

16:02.310 --> 16:04.020
D-Dojo challenge?

16:04.060 --> 16:07.820
<i>Takenaka Tsubaki</i>

16:04.440 --> 16:07.860
First up's the ace. I, Takenaka Tsubaki.

16:07.860 --> 16:11.190
<i>Takenaka Hiragi</i>

16:08.190 --> 16:11.240
Takenaka Hiiragi, also an ace!

16:11.320 --> 16:14.200
<i>Mimi Balguerie</i>

16:11.820 --> 16:14.240
I'm Mimi Balguerie, and I'm from France.

16:14.240 --> 16:17.080
<i>Fujii Masami</i>

16:14.660 --> 16:17.120
I'm the sniper, Fujii Masami.

16:17.120 --> 16:21.080
<i>Hakamada Kagetsu</i>

16:18.120 --> 16:21.120
I'm Nee-sama's younger sister, Hakamada Kagetsu...

16:21.620 --> 16:22.830
Ready and—

16:23.290 --> 16:25.290
With the five of us together,

16:25.290 --> 16:28.710
the New Keishin Academy
Mini Basketball Club is born!

16:35.050 --> 16:38.930
So that's why a match is going to be
held between the fifth and sixth years.

16:39.220 --> 16:40.060
Yep.

16:40.060 --> 16:42.890
With the winning team earning the right to use the gymnasium.

16:42.890 --> 16:44.560
I see.

16:45.060 --> 16:46.150
But above all,

16:46.150 --> 16:51.820
our girls are all pumped up with the appearance of a challenging team.

16:51.820 --> 16:55.360
Well, competition and maturity goes hand in hand, after all.

16:55.360 --> 16:59.780
It makes me want to go see Mimi-chan and Tomoka-chan's match.

16:59.780 --> 17:01.080
So, uh...

17:01.830 --> 17:04.370
I have a small request.

17:07.420 --> 17:09.790
I can't wait for the match on Friday.

17:09.790 --> 17:10.750
Me neither!

17:10.750 --> 17:13.630
Let's show them what we can do!

17:13.630 --> 17:18.220
Hey, Hina. Why did Kage join TsubaHii's team?

17:18.220 --> 17:19.510
Oh?

17:19.510 --> 17:21.720
Hina doesn't know either.

17:21.720 --> 17:26.480
But Hina would be happy to
have a match with Kage's team.

17:26.480 --> 17:27.770
I feel the same.

17:27.770 --> 17:31.940
Being friends again after having a serious match would be good.

17:31.940 --> 17:34.110
Let's do our best, everyone!

17:34.110 --> 17:35.950
All right!

17:48.170 --> 17:50.920
Okay, regarding today's match...

17:51.420 --> 17:53.460
I don't really have any instructions.

17:53.460 --> 17:56.670
Cooperate with one another, and match your rhythms.

17:57.220 --> 17:59.930
Tomoka, watch out for everyone.

17:59.930 --> 18:00.800
Yes, I will.

18:01.430 --> 18:03.720
Saki, I'm leaving the game plan to you.

18:03.720 --> 18:05.980
Form offensive patterns as you wish.

18:05.980 --> 18:06.810
Okay.

18:07.190 --> 18:09.690
Maho, grab all the points you can!

18:09.690 --> 18:11.270
Run wild with your instincts!

18:11.270 --> 18:12.110
Yeah!

18:12.110 --> 18:13.440
I'm really good at that!

18:13.940 --> 18:16.650
Airi, everyone's here for you.

18:16.650 --> 18:18.360
So don't hold back, and shoot.

18:18.360 --> 18:19.110
Okay!

18:19.110 --> 18:20.120
I'll do my best!

18:20.570 --> 18:24.200
Hinata-chan, let's surprise
Kagetsu-chan with what you can do!

18:24.200 --> 18:25.200
Oh!

18:25.200 --> 18:28.620
I'll do my very best to earn the
praise of both Kage and Onii-chan!

18:28.790 --> 18:32.000
Okay then, time for your match!

18:37.920 --> 18:38.590
Nice catch, Hina!

18:39.010 --> 18:39.630
Over here!

18:39.880 --> 18:40.890
Oh! Saki!

18:43.510 --> 18:46.560
Whoa, so you guys are out to get the ace, huh?

18:46.560 --> 18:48.350
We're not about to lose to you, stupid Maho!

19:03.950 --> 19:05.910
Why isn't anyone marking Kashii?!

19:06.290 --> 19:07.160
Kagetsu!

19:07.160 --> 19:08.120
Mark Kashii!

19:21.840 --> 19:24.350
Maho isn't enough of a player to warrant two markers!

19:32.350 --> 19:35.230
You need to stop focusing only on Saki's long shots!

19:35.480 --> 19:37.280
Oh man, seriously...

19:37.280 --> 19:38.650
Everyone's just doing what they want to.

19:38.650 --> 19:40.570
The whole thing's a mess.

19:40.570 --> 19:44.620
Organizing this team could be an incredibly tough task.

19:48.160 --> 19:48.620
Hii!

19:48.620 --> 19:49.750
All right!

19:55.540 --> 19:56.500
<i>Just as expected.</i>

19:56.500 --> 19:58.550
<i>The twins are in perfect sync.</i>

19:58.550 --> 20:00.800
6th Years

19:58.550 --> 20:00.800
5th Years

20:04.840 --> 20:05.260
Tsuba!

20:08.970 --> 20:09.720
H-Hii!

20:10.980 --> 20:12.230
Oh!

20:12.230 --> 20:13.440
Here comes Hina!

20:13.690 --> 20:15.440
Wh-What was that?!

20:16.020 --> 20:17.150
Here goes!

20:17.150 --> 20:19.190
It's Hina's turn!

20:19.480 --> 20:20.570
We have to stop her.

20:22.570 --> 20:23.360
Hina!

20:24.490 --> 20:25.240
Oh!

20:25.240 --> 20:27.410
Here it comes!

20:31.500 --> 20:33.410
Let's get them back.

20:35.210 --> 20:36.080
Wait a minute!

20:36.080 --> 20:38.210
What's with stealing your teammate's pass?

20:38.210 --> 20:40.210
Because the ball never gets passed to me.

20:42.760 --> 20:43.630
Tomoka!

20:43.630 --> 20:44.380
It's a challenge!

20:45.720 --> 20:46.550
However...

20:48.390 --> 20:51.640
We're not the only ones on the court right now!

20:51.640 --> 20:53.480
Right on!

20:53.480 --> 20:54.350
Hina!

20:55.520 --> 20:56.020
Oh!

20:56.900 --> 20:57.980
Wha—

21:00.110 --> 21:02.280
The point gap opened up again...

21:02.530 --> 21:04.360
What in the world are they doing?

21:04.360 --> 21:08.320
It's better to cool them down before it's too late.

21:08.320 --> 21:11.450
But even so, a team hastily put together like that...

21:11.450 --> 21:14.290
Y-You're telling me to do that?

21:15.420 --> 21:17.460
It's impossible for me.

21:17.460 --> 21:19.840
I don't even have any experience as a coach.

21:19.840 --> 21:22.130
It's true that it might be tough.

21:24.420 --> 21:26.300
Dad, you're late.

21:26.300 --> 21:27.430
Yeah, my bad.

21:27.430 --> 21:29.010
D-Dad?

21:30.510 --> 21:31.560
Time out!

21:32.310 --> 21:34.390
Everyone gather!

21:36.730 --> 21:37.400
Ginga!

21:37.600 --> 21:39.270
Subaru-san's dad!

21:42.610 --> 21:44.280
Listen up, everyone.

21:44.280 --> 21:49.450
It's been decided that I'll be the
fifth years' manager for the day!

21:50.830 --> 21:51.950
Nice meeting you guys!

21:51.950 --> 21:54.660
What?!

21:55.650 --> 21:58.400
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

21:58.400 --> 21:59.940
Rolling! Rolling!

21:59.940 --> 22:02.860
Keep on bouncing!

22:01.150 --> 22:03.870
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

22:03.870 --> 22:06.280
Elementary schoolers are the best!

22:06.280 --> 22:06.660
Yay!

22:10.750 --> 22:15.750
Our bodies and our hearts are size SS,

22:16.250 --> 22:21.670
but our dreams can be size LL, can't they? Can't they?

22:21.670 --> 22:27.060
Adolescents have lots of troubles,

22:27.060 --> 22:32.640
but we'll overcome them together.

22:32.640 --> 22:38.070
I want to get even better!

22:33.440 --> 22:34.810
Even

22:34.810 --> 22:36.150
better!

22:38.070 --> 22:45.740
I want to see your face when I surprise you!

22:39.030 --> 22:39.690
Ooh!

22:40.360 --> 22:41.070
Wow!

22:45.950 --> 22:48.660
Just keep on spinning!

22:48.660 --> 22:52.580
The Earth is one big basketball!

22:52.580 --> 22:56.250
I'll believe in the future and move forward!

22:55.630 --> 22:57.170
I'll keep going!

22:56.880 --> 22:59.590
Just keep on spinning!

22:59.590 --> 23:03.550
The universe is one big basketball court!

23:03.550 --> 23:06.970
I want you to receive it.

23:06.260 --> 23:07.220
Ready, and!

23:06.970 --> 23:08.810
Pass! Pass! Pass!

23:09.220 --> 23:11.220
Please take it!

23:12.480 --> 23:15.230
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

23:15.230 --> 23:16.770
Rolling! Rolling!

23:16.770 --> 23:19.650
Keep on bouncing!

23:17.900 --> 23:20.650
Rolling! Rolling! Growing!

23:20.650 --> 23:23.110
Elementary schoolers are the best!

23:23.110 --> 23:23.940
Yay!

23:25.420 --> 23:28.340
We got to meet Hasegawa-san's dad today.

23:28.340 --> 23:29.260
Oh!

23:29.260 --> 23:30.720
Onii-chan's daddy!

23:30.720 --> 23:31.720
Dandyism?

23:31.720 --> 23:33.390
What does that mean?

23:33.390 --> 23:34.050
Oh.

23:34.050 --> 23:35.260
I don't really know.

23:35.260 --> 23:36.430
It's confusing, yes.

23:36.430 --> 23:37.520
Confusing.

23:37.060 --> 23:40.060
Paradigm Ginga

23:37.060 --> 23:40.060
Next episode

23:37.520 --> 23:39.430
Hmm...
